 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Generic replacement in degrees at least two",
 "statement": "Let $C/k$ be a smooth integral separated\ncurve over algebraically closed $k$,\nand let $\\eta:\\operatorname{Spec}k(C)\\to C$ be its generic point,\nwith function field $k(C)$.\nFor every torsion etale sheaf\n$F$, the adjunction map induces\n\n$$\nH^q(C,F)\\ \\xrightarrow{\\ \\sim\\ }\\ H^q(C,\\eta_*\\eta^*F)\n\\qquad(q\\geq2)\n$$\n\non cohomology.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-curve-estimates/sk-prop-cd/lem-sc-generic-cohomology-comparison.md",
  "place": "node lem-sc-generic-cohomology-comparison, order 1005"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-sc-curves",
  "def-sc-function-field",
  "def-weil-pbc-etale-cohomology",
  "def-weil-pbc-etale-sheaves"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The generic restriction of $\\eta_*M$ is $M$: after a geometric\ngeneric base change the source is the same separably closed\npoint, as is also seen in\n[prop-weil-pbc-strict-henselization-stalk-formula] in degree zero.\nHence the kernel and cokernel of $F\\to\\eta_*\\eta^*F$ both\nhave zero generic restriction. They are acyclic by\n[lem-sc-zero-generic-acyclic]. Write the map as a\nsurjection onto its image followed by an injection. The two\nlong exact sequences give the displayed isomorphism for $q\\geq2$.",
   "uses": [
    "prop-weil-pbc-strict-henselization-stalk-formula",
    "lem-sc-zero-generic-acyclic"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
